Z||000006||mrfiero||01-04-2000||04:32 AM||||In all fairness, if you order a new auto. shift handle from GM it is over $100.  I bought one for my '88 GT (tan interior) to have as a spare and paid $100+ for it (can't remember exact price).<P>Also, the INDY nose emblem is made out of metal, not plastic like all other Fieros, and is super hard to find used, let alone brand new. <P>Don't get me wrong, I too think these prices are too high.<BR> <BR>In any business you will find some cheap prices and some high prices, but the majority will lie somewhere in between.  This place is just one of those on the high side.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||01-04-2000||05:00 AM||||If you don't like the T type shifter handle for the auto, you can get a leather covered one for a Camaro Z28 brand new for less than $50 through GM.  Just a note. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
